# Environment configuration — application.
#
# Copy to `.env` (or `.env.local` for the app) and fill in locally.
# `.env*` is git-ignored; this file is the committed template.
#
# Only variables the application itself needs are listed. Product secrets are
# deliberately ABSENT and must be added when the feature that needs them is
# implemented — not speculatively. See .agents/rules/01-source-of-truth-and-scope.md.
#
# The Flutterwave block below is the one exception to that rule, and it is no longer
# speculative: the payment endpoints are implemented, so the variables they read are
# documented here. They are NOT required for startup — `getServerEnv()` reads only
# `DATABASE_URL`, and the payment variables are read lazily by `getPaymentEnv()` the
# first time a payment endpoint is actually used. A deployment with an optional
# feature unconfigured still boots, and a payment endpoint called without them fails
# loudly, by variable name, rather than failing obscurely later.
#
# There is deliberately NO session secret. Sessions are opaque random tokens
# stored as a SHA-256 hash and matched by lookup, so there is no signing key to
# provision, rotate, or leak.

# PostgreSQL connection string.
# Consumed by:
#   - prisma.config.ts  (Prisma CLI: migrate, generate)
#   - src/server/env.ts (application runtime, via the pg driver adapter)
#
# `options=-c timezone=UTC` is REQUIRED, not cosmetic. It pins each connection's
# session time zone to UTC so absolute instants round-trip correctly regardless of
# the server's or the host's local zone. Without it, Prisma's write path sends the
# UTC wall clock as a *naive* timestamp that PostgreSQL then reinterprets in the
# session zone, storing every `timestamptz` shifted by that offset (observed: one
# hour early on an Africa/Lagos host). Write and read are symmetric, so
# Prisma-only round-trip tests still pass and the corruption is invisible from the
# ORM. Pinned by tests/events.db.test.ts ("stores the instant the organiser actually
# submitted"), which asserts against ground truth read by an independent client.
#
# Store UTC, render in the viewer's timezone. See .agents/rules/02-domain-model-and-data-integrity.md.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@localhost:5432/DATABASE_NAME?schema=public&options=-c%20timezone%3DUTC"

# --- Flutterwave (PRD v2 §8, §12) -------------------------------------------
# Consumed by:
#   - src/server/env.ts (getPaymentEnv(), read at first use)
#   - src/server/flutterwave/client.ts (the two secrets)
#   - src/server/flutterwave/webhook.ts (the webhook secret)
#   - src/server/flutterwave/redirect-url.ts (the redirect origin)
#
# Both secrets are REQUIRED together: the payment endpoints cannot verify anything
# without them, and a deployment missing one fails on the first payment call with the
# missing name in the message. Values here are placeholders — never commit a real
# secret. `FLUTTERWAVE_SECRET_KEY` is the secret key from the provider dashboard, and
# `FLUTTERWAVE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is the `verif-hash` value the provider signs webhooks
# with; they are different values and using one for both makes every delivery fail
# authentication.
FLUTTERWAVE_SECRET_KEY=""
FLUTTERWAVE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# Override the live API base. Almost never set in production: the default is
# https://api.flutterwave.com/v3. It exists so a test can point the adapter at a stub
# instead of the internet.
FLUTTERWAVE_API_BASE_URL="https://api.flutterwave.com/v3"

# The PUBLIC origin to send the attendee back to after hosted checkout, e.g.
# "https://tickets.example.com" — an origin, not the verify path.
#
# OPTIONAL, and absent is a supported state: with no public origin configured the
# payment still completes, driven by the webhook alone, which PRD v2 §8.6 makes the
# governing channel. The path is appended by the application
# (`/api/v1/payments/verify`); a full path here is accepted and left alone.
#
# Present but not an absolute http(s) URL is NOT supported: such a value would be
# sent to the provider and then fail at the attendee, after a hold had been taken, so
# it is rejected when the variable is read. Leave empty to run webhook-only.
FLUTTERWAVE_REDIRECT_BASE_URL=""
